# sidgwick over the corpus's shared atoms, written by phil/corpus from readings/sidgwick/logic: not to be edited
atom	proven_visible(x)	proof can be given that x is visible
atom	seen(x)	people actually see x
atom	proven_audible(x)	proof can be given that x is audible
atom	heard(x)	people hear x
atom	proven_desirable_cap(x)	evidence can be produced that x is desirable, in the sense of capable of being desired, by analogy with visible and audible
atom	desired(x)	people do actually desire x
atom	acknowledged_end(x)	x is acknowledged, in theory and in practice, to be an end
atom	convincible_end(x)	some person could be convinced that x is an end
atom	reason_desirable_good(x)	a reason can be given why x is desirable, in the sense of worth desiring
atom	person(x)	x is a person
atom	desires_own_happiness(x)	x desires his own happiness, so far as he believes it attainable
atom	full_proof_good(x)	we have all the proof the case admits of, and all it is possible to require, that x is a good
atom	good(x)	x is a good
atom	own_happiness_good(x)	x's happiness is a good to x
atom	good_to_aggregate(x)	x is a good to the aggregate of all persons
atom	end_of_conduct(x)	x has made out its title as one of the ends of conduct
atom	criterion_of_morality(x)	x is one of the criteria of morality
atom	sidgwick_desires_general(x)	x has an actual desire for the general happiness
atom	sidgwick_ought_aim_general	each individual ought to desire, or aim at realising in action, the general happiness
atom	sidgwick_means_ought	by "the general happiness is desirable" Mill means that it is what each individual ought to desire or aim at
atom	sidgwick_established	the proposition that the general happiness is desirable (in the ought sense) is established by Mill's reasoning
atom	sidgwick_gap	there is a gap in Mill's expressed argument
atom	sidgwick_only_benevolence_fills	the gap can only be filled by some such proposition as the intuition of Rational Benevolence
P1	S7	∀x (proven_desirable_cap(x) → desired(x))	says mill
P2	S8	reason_desirable_good(gh) → ∀x (person(x) → desires_own_happiness(x))	says mill
P3	S9	∀x (person(x) → desires_own_happiness(x)) → full_proof_good(happiness) ∧ ∀x (person(x) → own_happiness_good(x)) ∧ good_to_aggregate(gh)	says mill
P4	S11	sidgwick_means_ought	kind conceptual
P5	S13	∀x (person(x) → ¬desires_general(x))
P6	S14	∀x (person(x) → ¬desires_general(x)) → ¬sidgwick_established
P7	S14	¬sidgwick_established → sidgwick_gap
P8	S14	sidgwick_only_benevolence_fills
C1	S12	¬sidgwick_established	from P5 P6
C	S14	sidgwick_gap	from C1 P7
